  - "src/effect/**"
  - "src/github/**"
  - "test/prSurfaceImportGraph.test.ts"
  - "test/prSurface.seam.test.ts"
---

All GitHub REST I/O for a pull request goes through `createPrSurface` / `PrSurface` in `src/github/prSurface.ts` (ADR 0026). Outside `src/github/` (plus `src/prWorkspace/` for checkout credentials) there is no `@octokit/*` import, no `installationOctokit` reference, and no exported signature carrying `token: string`, `expiresAtTs`, or `tokenExpiresAtTs`; `test/prSurfaceImportGraph.test.ts` scans every `src/` file for exactly those. Work items store `installationId`, and the worker mints the token inside the seam at execution time. `gitCredentialAuth()` is the only credential escape, used for clone and push. Leased executors receive the epoch-aware surface so each method in `PR_SURFACE_MUTATION_METHODS` runs inside the operation-intent boundary and recovers through `recoverPrSurfaceMutation.ts`; never import `prSurfaceImpl.ts` from feature or worker code. Fake with `createFakePrSurface` (`src/github/fakePrSurface.ts`); do not mock Octokit in feature tests.
